The growing demand for compact electronic devices, higher memory capacity and efficient semiconductor packaging is supporting the Multiple Chip Package (MCP) Market. As smartphones, connected devices, industrial electronics and edge-computing systems incorporate more functionality into limited board space, MCP technology provides a way to integrate multiple semiconductor dies within a single package.

According to Semiconductor Insight, the global Multiple Chip Package Market was valued at USD 2.673 billion in 2025 and is projected to reach USD 5.850 billion by 2034, expanding at a CAGR of 9.1% during the 2026–2034 forecast period. Asia Pacific held the largest regional position in the report's coverage, supported by semiconductor packaging capacity and the region's extensive electronics manufacturing ecosystem.

Multiple chip packages combine two or more semiconductor dies within one package to reduce footprint and simplify system integration. Memory-oriented MCP solutions may combine DRAM with NAND flash or managed storage, allowing device manufacturers to reduce board space while maintaining the memory capacity required by compact products.

